Let the secondary side bar stack with the primary side bar.

This adds an opt-in setting for Canvas-style dense layouts:
`workbench.sideBar.experimental.splitWithSecondarySideBar`.
When enabled, the primary side bar and secondary side bar share one vertical
column, so users can keep two side-bar containers visible at once (for example
Explorer above Projects). This takes precedence over the bottom-pane split
setting because the secondary side bar can only occupy one split target.

